@zeripath ok for me, makes sense.

Only checking for the "off" is enough, not? code could be a bit more readable like this

```go
if valueInSlice("off", SSH.AuthorizedPrincipalsAllow) {
   SSH.AuthorizedPrincipalsAllow="off"
}
```

```go
func valueInSlice(value string, slice []string) bool {
	for _, v := range slice {
		v = strings.ToLower(strings.TrimSpace(v))
		if v == value {
			return true
		}
	}

	return false
}
```


Also the `len(setting.SSH.AuthorizedPrincipalsAllow) > 0` check can be removed because it always will be > 0
(that check also isn't done in the `setting.go`)

Or we could also add another bool only used internally  `SSH.AuthorizedPrincipalsEnabled`
